---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **K팝 아이돌 생일은 달마다 고른가.** (`/kpop-birthdays`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면이 있나 ─────────────────────────────────────────
 *   Search Console 28일치(2026-08-04~09-01)에서 손님이 이렇게 묻는다 —
 *     「kpop birthdays in january」 자리 69.0 · 「kpop idol born in july」 자리 82.0
 *     「skz birthday」 65.5 · 「ateez birthdays」 76.0 · 「katseye members birthdays」 77.5
 *   자리가 65~82 다. 사실상 «없는» 답이다. 우리는 1,295명의 생일을 쥐고 있다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **그냥 세지 않는다.** 달마다 날수가 달라 2월이 늘 적게 나온다 — «하루당»으로 고른다.
 * ⛔ 🔴 **1월 1일을 그대로 세지 않는다.** 13명이 몰려 있고 그것은 하루평균의 3.67배다.
 *    «생년만 알 때 채우는 날»이다. 뺀 값을 나란히 싣고, 뺀 뒤에도 결과가 사는지 보인다.
 * ⛔ **「왜 그런가」를 말하지 않는다.** 출생 계절성인지 명단이 치우친 것인지 못 갈랐다.
 * ⛔ 평균만 앞세우지 않는다 — 달마다의 수를 전부 표로 싣는다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 TypeScript 다. JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-kpop-birthday-months.json';
/* 날짜 지면(/born-on)이 몇 명을 담는지 — 우리 두 수가 왜 다른지 밝히는 데 쓴다 */
import 날짜지면 from '../../data/wikitip-birthday-pages.json';

const 뺀것 = d.한날뺀것;
const 시험 = d.시험한날뺀것;
const 가장많은달 = [...뺀것.달들].sort((a, b) => b.하루당 - a.하루당)[0];
const 가장적은달 = [...뺀것.달들].sort((a, b) => a.하루당 - b.하루당)[0];

/* 🔴 [2026-09-09] 넓은 명부(연예인 전체)를 나란히 싣는다 — 답이 «다르다».
 *   ⛔ 옛 표를 갈아 치우지 않는다. 둘을 함께 두어야 「어느 명부냐」를 묻게 된다.
 *   ⛔ 넓은명부가 없으면 그 절을 «안 낸다». 없는 것을 0 으로 채우지 않는다. */
const 넓은 = d.넓은명부 ?? null;
const 하루당순 = (x) => [...x.달들].sort((a, b) => b.하루당 - a.하루당);
const 넓1위 = 넓은 ? 하루당순(넓은.전부)[0] : null;
const 넓꼴찌 = 넓은 ? 하루당순(넓은.전부).at(-1) : null;
const 넓뺀1위 = 넓은 ? 하루당순(넓은.몰린날여럿뺀것)[0] : null;
const 넓뺀꼴찌 = 넓은 ? 하루당순(넓은.몰린날여럿뺀것).at(-1) : null;
/* ⭐ 정정에 쓰는 «옛 수»는 손으로 적는다 — 자료에 남아 있지 않은 값이다.
 *   ⚠ 손으로 적은 것임을 여기 밝혀 둔다. 다음 사람이 이것을 실측으로 오해하지 않게. */
const 옛사람수 = '1,295';
/* ⛔ 날짜 지면 사람 수를 손으로 적지 않는다 — 그 지면 자료에서 읽는다.
 *   손으로 적으면 그 지면이 늘 때 이 줄이 조용히 낡는다. */
const 날짜지면사람수 = Number(날짜지면.peopleListed ?? 0).toLocaleString('en-US');

const TITLE = `K-pop idol birthdays by month: July is the thinnest, March the fullest`;
const DESC = `${뺀것.합} K-pop group members with a birth date on record. `
  + `March has ${가장많은달.고른값의배}x an even month, July ${가장적은달.고른값의배}x. `
  + `Every month listed, with the noise test.`;

const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org'],
  license: 'https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/',
}];
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/kpop-birthdays">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Which month has the most K-pop idol birthdays? We counted every member of the{' '}
    {d.그룹수} K-pop groups we hold — {뺀것.합} people with a birth date on record.
  </p>

  <p class="q">
    Months are not the same length, so counting raw totals makes February look small every time.
    Each month below is put on a per-day footing first. An even year would give every month{' '}
    <strong>1.00x</strong>. March comes out at <strong>{가장많은달.고른값의배}x</strong> and July at{' '}
    <strong>{가장적은달.고른값의배}x</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Every month</h2>
  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Month</th><th>Members</th><th>Share</th><th>Per day</th><th>vs an even month</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {뺀것.달들.map((m) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{m.달}</th>
            <td>{m.수}</td>
            <td>{m.몫}%</td>
            <td>{m.하루당}</td>
            <td>{m.고른값의배}x</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
      <tfoot>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">All twelve</th>
          <td>{뺀것.합}</td>
          <td>100%</td>
          <td>{(뺀것.합 / 365.2425).toFixed(3)}</td>
          <td>1.00x</td>
        </tr>
      </tfoot>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Is that just chance?</h2>
  <p class="q">
    With {뺀것.합} people spread over twelve months, some months will run ahead of others by luck
    alone. So we scattered the same number of birthdays evenly across the year{' '}
    {시험.횟수.toLocaleString('en-US')} times, with a fixed seed ({시험.씨앗}) so anyone re-running
    this gets the same figure, and asked how often the gap between the fullest and thinnest month
    came out as wide as ours. It did <strong>{시험.우연일확률}%</strong> of the time.
  </p>
  <p class="q">
    {시험.못쟀다고적어야하나
      ? 'That is above our 5% line, so we do not say the months differ.'
      : 'That is below our 5% line, so the gap is not explained by chance alone. What causes it, we did not measure.'}
  </p>

  <h2>One date we had to remove</h2>
  <p class="q">
    Before any of the above, we took out <strong>1 January</strong>. It held{' '}
    {d.몰린날[0].수} people — <strong>{d.몰린날[0].하루평균의배} times</strong> an average day.
    That is the date sources use when only the birth year is known, so it is a record-keeping
    artefact rather than a run of January births. Including it, the chance figure was{' '}
    {d.시험전부.우연일확률}%; removing it, {시험.우연일확률}%. The finding survives either way,
    but the honest table is the one without it.
  </p>

  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Members</th><th>vs an average day</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.몰린날.map((x) => (
          <tr><th scope="row">{x.날}</th><td>{x.수}</td><td>{x.하루평균의배}x</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  {넓은 && (
    <section>
      <h2>A wider panel gives a different answer — {넓은.사람수.toLocaleString('en-US')} people</h2>
      <p class="q">
        Everything above counts <strong>group members</strong>. We also hold a birth date for{' '}
        <strong>{넓은.사람수.toLocaleString('en-US')} Korean entertainers</strong> — actors and solo
        artists included, not only people in groups. Run the same method on that panel and the
        answer changes: <strong>{넓1위.달}</strong> is the fullest month at{' '}
        <strong>{넓1위.고른값의배}x</strong> an even month, and <strong>{넓꼴찌.달}</strong> the
        thinnest at <strong>{넓꼴찌.고른값의배}x</strong>.
      </p>
      <p class="warn">
        <b>The two panels disagree, and we print both rather than retiring one.</b> The group
        table says {가장많은달.달} and {가장적은달.달}; the wider table says {넓1위.달} and{' '}
        {넓꼴찌.달}. Neither is wrong — they answer different questions. But it means
        “the month with the most K-pop birthdays” is not a sentence anybody can finish without
        first saying which panel they mean.
      </p>
      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Month</th><th>People</th><th>Per day</th><th>vs an even month</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {넓은.전부.달들.map((m) => (
              <tr class={m.달 === 넓1위.달 || m.달 === 넓꼴찌.달 ? 'edge' : ''}>
                <th scope="row">{m.달}</th>
                <td>{m.수.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
                <td>{m.하루당}</td>
                <td>{m.고른값의배}x</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="q">
        The noise test on this panel returns <strong>{넓은.시험전부.우연일확률}%</strong>, so the
        spread is not explained by chance. <b>Why</b> it happens we did not measure, and the
        candidates — birth seasonality, school-entry cutoffs, and who ends up with a Wikidata
        entry at all — would each produce this shape.
      </p>
      <p class="q">
        <b>We deleted the crowded days and re-counted.</b> Five dates hold more than 1.5 times an
        average day, led by 1 January and 28 February at the same height. Removing all five —{' '}
        {넓은.몰린날여럿뺀것.뺀사람.toLocaleString('en-US')} people — leaves {넓뺀1위.달} first at{' '}
        {넓뺀1위.하루당} per day and {넓뺀꼴찌.달} last at {넓뺀꼴찌.하루당}. The threshold picked
        the dates, not us.
      </p>
      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>People</th><th>vs an average day</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {넓은.몰린날.map((x) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{x.날}</th><td>{x.수}</td><td>{x.하루평균의배}x</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {넓은.날별 && (
        <div>
          <h3>Every calendar day</h3>
          <p class="q">
            All <strong>{넓은.날별.날칸수}</strong> dates, including 29 February. An average date
            holds <strong>{넓은.날별.하루평균}</strong> people. Rank is shared, so two dates with
            the same count get the same place. <b>A date with nobody on it would show 0, not
            vanish</b> — as it happens, every date in the year has at least one.
          </p>
          <p class="q">
            <b>Our day pages give a smaller number for the same date, on purpose.</b> The{' '}
            <a href="/born-on/10-13">born-on pages</a> cover {날짜지면사람수} people who have an
            English Wikipedia article, because they rank the day's names by reads. This table
            covers {넓은.사람수.toLocaleString('en-US')} people who have a birth date recorded at
            all. Wider panel, larger count — the two are answering different questions, and
            neither is a correction of the other.
          </p>
          <div class="scroll-x tall">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>People</th><th>Rank of {넓은.날별.날칸수}</th><th>vs an average day</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {넓은.날별.날들.map((x) => (
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row"><a href={`/born-on/${x.날}`}>{x.날}</a></th>
                    <td>{x.수}</td>
                    <td>{x.자리}</td>
                    <td>{x.하루평균의배}x</td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      )}
    </section>
  )}

  <section>
    <h2>Correction, 9 September 2026</h2>
    <p class="warn">
      <b>This page said {옛사람수} people until today. It now says {뺀것.합}.</b> We were
      de-duplicating people by name, which merged different people who happen to share one —
      in the wider panel above, 288 names carry more than one birth date. The count is now keyed
      on the record identifier where there is one, and on name plus birth date where there is
      not. The month ranking on this page did not change; the number of people did, and we are
      not going to swap a published figure without saying so.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>What this is not</h2>
  <p class="q">
    This is a count of {뺀것.합} people, not a statement about anyone. It does not say a month is
    lucky, and it does not say why the months differ — seasonal birth patterns in Korea and the
    way our roster was assembled would both produce a gap like this, and we did not separate them.
    Birth dates come from Wikidata (property P569), which is CC0. Members whose birth date is not
    recorded there are not in the count at all: we hold{' '}
    {d.멤버자리} member places across {d.그룹수} groups, and {뺀것.합} people survived after
    removing duplicates and the 1 January artefact.
  </p>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/kpop-birthdays" />
</WikiTip>
